  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column of the governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (pp6-7). Beginning fund balance 7,466,375 is as originally reported; the 359,920 restatement is an adjustment (as restated 7,826,295); reconciles to ending 7,601,029. ending_cash = Cash and cash equivalents, Total Governmental Funds column of the balance sheet (p4-5; excludes county treasurer cash 94,540 and restricted cash 7,325,821). Business-type from the Total enterprise funds column (pp10-11, excludes Internal Service Funds): net position 44,848,764 to 46,135,911 reconciles using transfers (2,278,500) and gain on sale 71,410 (other_financing). Proprietary cash flows from Total column (pp12-13), operating/noncapital/capital/investing; beginning cash 16,118,258 and ending 13,982,560 as printed. Balance sheet is the government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1); interfund due to/from lines net to zero in Total column and are omitted; Land and construction in progress combined as printed. Detail: Budgetary comparison schedules (budget basis, so actuals differ slightly from the GAAP statement, e.g. General Fund 3,431,512 vs 3,426,669) for General, Street, Sales Tax, Debt Service, Redevelopment and Airport funds; nonmajor combining schedule (15 funds) recorded with its Total column as Nonmajor funds (combined). Zero-actual lines omitted (e.g. Redevelopment bond/loan proceeds, Airport transfers in, Street sale of property); Redevelopment prints no expenditure total and Sales Tax/Debt Service have no spending. Trimmed pp14-15 (gained in v7 re-trim, original pp32-33) are the proprietary cash flow statement's reconciliation of operating income to operating cash flow; nothing new to record. Read pages 1-25 of 25"
}